{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Hereby you shall know that YHWH sent me to do all these deeds.</b> To substitute the Levites for the firstborn, because the firstborn were disqualified by the sin of the calf, as it is written (Exodus 32:6): ״ויעלו עולות ויגישו שלמים״ — and those who offered were the firstborn; and the children of Levi, who were cleansed of that sin and who slew the worshippers of the calf, were sanctified in place of the firstborn and chosen for the service of YHWH. And anyone who did not believe in the election of the Levites and their substitution in place of the firstborn was testifying against himself that the sin of the calf had not been accounted settled before the Holy One, blessed be He — and this is a grievous sin and a contradiction of the verses."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The text reads הש\"י; resolved as the standard abbreviation for הקב\"ה הוא שמית (or similar reverent circumlocution), rendered here 'the Holy One, blessed be He' to match the prescribed register for reverent abbreviations."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:14.511113527Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}